Thu Oct 22 2026  Corkscrew maintainers
	* Integrated handshake output with the duplex relay, preserving
	  coalesced tunnel bytes and remote half-close semantics.
	* Added signal cleanup for SIGQUIT and SIGTSTP, prevented proxy
	  socket collisions with standard descriptors, and centralized
	  credential clearing and descriptor teardown.
	* Enforced safe authentication-file permissions and types.
	* Wired the Python regression suite into make check and distcheck,
	  added strict CI builds and sanitizer coverage, and installed a
	  corkscrew(1) manual page.
	* Added --help, --version, --verbose, connect/handshake timeout
	  options, --auth-file, inherited --auth-fd, and opt-in HTTP/1.1
	  CONNECT headers.
	* Added tinyproxy loopback integration, libFuzzer parser coverage,
	  macOS portability CI, and release version 3.0.
	* Made README.md canonical, added CHANGELOG.md, and updated the
	  manual page, NEWS, and security documentation.

